<CLAIM evidence_lines="30, 36, 39, 42, 43, 45, 47, 49, 52, 53, 70, 71, 73">
mechanism: The socket obtained via sockfd_lookup (line 30) is stored into sdev->ud.tcp_socket/sockfd (lines 42-43) and the lock is released (line 45) before the rx/tx threads are started (lines 47-50); the status is only set to SDEV_ST_USED afterward (line 53). A concurrent 'stub down' path (sockfd == -1) can observe SDEV_ST_USED and trigger SDEV_EVENT_DOWN, tearing down the socket/threads while this path still uses them, and the error path at sock_err/err (lines 70-73) also unlocks the spinlock that was already unlocked at line 45, causing a double-unlock. The attacker-controlled sockfd from sscanf (line 14) drives this state machine.
</CLAIM>

